cal checks. The develop branch is not a stable evaluation baseline.","limitations","guidance","list","Setup","ordered",true,"items",[73,74,75],"setup","Select a release tag, install its supported Unity editor and open the included Project.","Install the matching com.unity.ml-agents package and Python environment package versions.","Open an example scene and connect a policy; route actions by behavior and agent_id, and read both DecisionSteps and TerminalSteps. Python step advances to the next decision, not necessarily one physics frame.","Try these tasks",false,[80,81,82],"testTasks","Compare physics-task success with fixed observations, decisions and reset rules.","Change a C# agent or scene and verify sensors, rewards and episode termination.","Import a replacement rig or collider and check control stability and visual observations.","AI use and evaluation boundary","The toolkit supports agent research and automated testing; its Apache license does not replace editor or third-party asset terms.","aiUseNote","links","Supporting evidence",[90,91,92,93],"evidence",{"_54":100,"_25":101},{"_54":98,"_25":99},{"_54":96,"_25":97},{"_54":94,"_25":95},"Unity editor terms","https://unity.com/legal/editor-terms-of-service/software","Third-party notices","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/blob/develop/Third%20Party%20Notices.md","Release 23 low-level decision and terminal contract","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/blob/a2777719560e4676be99e2ea128c5eb1fbeb3dbb/com.unity.ml-agents/Documentation~/Python-LLAPI.md","Official toolkit and release compatibility","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents#readme","Read the terms",[105],"licenseUrl",{"_54":102,"_25":106},"https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/blob/develop/LICENSE.md","Terms category","Engine-specific terms","terms","provenance","Asset license","Check bundled notices and any added scene assets. The Unity editor and external store assets have separate terms.","assetLicense","C